## 4. Deployment Topology (Fly.io)

### 4.1 Single App Layout

- **Single Fly app** with:
  - One process: `web`
  - Runs Uvicorn or Gunicorn + Uvicorn worker
  - Serves:
    - `/api/*` → FastAPI routes
    - `/ws/*` → WebSockets
    - `/` → Frontend SPA (static assets)

### 4.2 Process Command (example)

```toml
# fly.toml (simplified sketch)
[build]
  # Docker or builder settings here

[env]
  APP_ENV = "production"

[http_service]
  internal_port = 8000
  force_https = true

[processes]
  web = "uvicorn src.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000"

(Exact fly.toml will be fleshed out later.)

4.3 Static Frontend

Frontend built into a dist/ folder (Vite or similar)

Backend serves static files:

GET / and other non-API routes → index.html

GET /assets/* → built JS/CSS files




