7. Core Data Model (High-Level)

7.1 Entities (Nodes)

Typical labels:

Character

Location

Faction

Item

Event

Concept


Each with:

Required properties (id, name, description, etc.)

Optional properties (depending on templates)

Provenance metadata (source text, confidence, timestamps)


Special properties:

Character:

ocean: { O, C, E, A, N }

Potential additional personality metadata later



7.2 Relationships

Examples:

(:Character)-[:MEMBER_OF]->(:Faction)

(:Character)-[:LOCATED_IN]->(:Location)

(:Faction)-[:ENEMY_OF]->(:Faction)

(:Event)-[:OCCURS_AT]->(:Location)

(:Character)-[:PARTICIPATED_IN]->(:Event)


7.3 Embeddings

Vector representation of entities for semantic search

Stored in a vector index (e.g., entity_embeddings)

Allows QueryAgent to find relevant entities by meaning, not exact string match



